<title>UK: SBC Jersey sets $200 million three-year bond.</title>
<headline>SBC Jersey sets $200 million three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWISS BANK CORP (JERSEY)</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     6.00	MATURITY    24.JUL.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.8025  PAY DATE    24.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.615    SPREAD	+2 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS</p>
<p>US/UK/JESY</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.1875    SELL CONC  1.1875    PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.375 PCT MAY 2000 U.S.T</p>
<p> NOTES	UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED</p>
<p>		LAUNCHED UNDER ISSUER'S DEBT SECURITIES PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
